description:
FILED + FIXED s518e (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-17) from the Type-Tiny census: after #3401 the "Not a type library" files died "Could not load library 'DemoLib': Could not find parent type" -- `declare "Number", as "String", where {...}` with Type::Utils's `sub as (@) { parent => @_; }` / `sub where (&;@) { constraint => @_; }`.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 vs main ff4c1500):

    sub h { ("b", "c") }  sub g { "a", h() }  sub mm { "a", @_ }
    sub id { @_ }  sub cnt { scalar(@_) }
    print join(" ", id(mm(1, 2)), "|", id(g()), "|", cnt(mm(1,2)), cnt(g())), "\n";

perl: `a 1 2 | a b c | 3 3`.  PCL: `a ARRAY(0x1) | a ARRAY(0x2) | 2 2`.  A direct `my @x = g()` was right (the assignment flattens deeper), which hid it; `return (LIST)` was always right.

CAUSE: Pl/ExprToCL.pm gen_progn_form's VOID/INHERIT branch (a body's tail list) built `(if *wantarray* (vector …) …)` wrapping only Symbol-shaped arrays in a p-flatten MARKER; `@_` (a Magic token) and a call's vector went in raw, and a marker / vector element stays ONE element when the value is spread as call arguments (p-flatten-args spreads one level).  The marker for `@G` leaked too (cnt(k()) counted 2) and could print into eval'd code.

FIX: the branch builds the list exactly as the LIST_CTX branch does -- all provably scalar -> (vector …), else (p-flatten-args (list list …)).  ir-spec §5 normative paragraph; Pl/t/return-copy-01.t comment updated (its rows pass).  Generation v2-6684.  Perf: a tail list with a non-scalar element now pays p-flatten-args in list context (it paid the vector before) -- Fable to decide whether a re-bench is owed.

GUARD: Pl/t/tail-return-01.t row 10, inverse-verified on a main extraction.
